# Situation

Repo: claude-engineering-skills (public upstream). Besides skills it ships a tooling bundle that its sync script copies into consumer repos. In a consumer every `scripts/<x>` file lands at `scripts/.claude-skills/<x>` (one directory deeper) and the consumer runs it there; the same file in this repo runs at `scripts/<x>`. Files the sync copies are: everything reachable by static `import` from the sync's entry lists (an import-graph walk), plus an explicit list of files that are read at runtime by path and so cannot be found by the walk (`CORE_ASSETS`, shown below). A second, hand-maintained mirror of that list lives in `sync-inventory.mjs` (used by the verifier and other tooling).

The change under review (PR #351, pre-merge, CI green on the PR head) fixes a misleading dashboard figure: two "standing queue" counts come from database views that are rolling windows on `audit_runs.created_at`, so a fall between two readings is rows ageing out, not work done. It adds a gate, a rule in a reference doc, a declaration file at the repo root (`.windowed-views.json`, which names the windowed views and which dashboard queues each one backs), and the dashboard change below: for a queue the declaration marks as windowed, the dashboard withholds the previous value so the chip is neutral; if the declaration cannot be read, it withholds the trend for every queue. The dashboard is part of the bundle consumers receive and run against their own `status.md` and the shared store.

The author's own tests run in this repo. No consumer has this code yet. You are asked to review before merge.

